 "finding": "LABELLED DEVIATION, NOT THE PUBLISHED MODEL. Excitatory synapses depress with use. The two constants are measured (ORN->PN, glomeruli DM6 and VM2: f=0.78, tau=893 ms; ORN->LN (GABAergic antennal-lobe local neurons): f=0.75, tau=1566 ms; ORN->PN, glomerulus DM4: f=0.72, tau=2400 ms). The published model has no synaptic dynamics beyond a 5 ms conductance decay, and adding depression changes what a synapse is, so no run with it switched on is a property of the published model. Beyond that, the measurements are at ORN to PN and ORN to LN synapses only. Applying the same two constants to any other synapse is an extrapolation the measurements do not license, which is why the scope is an arm of the experiment and not a setting. The brain has up and down states in 0 of 9 runs and the trained Kenyon-cell ensemble in 6. Every constant behind the mechanism is measured; the scope is an arm and the arms are reported separately, because the recordings are at ORN to PN and ORN to LN synapses and say nothing about any other synapse.",
